TeslaSync.App.UITests.dll : Failed! - Failed: 147, Passed: 0, Total: 147, Duration: ~228 ms
Root cause (identical for all 147): UiAutomationUnavailableException --
  "UI automation cannot run: WinAppDriver/Appium runner is absent: nothing is listening on
   http://127.0.0.1:4723/ and WinAppDriver.exe was not found at its standard install paths or on PATH."
  (WinAppDriverSession.EnsureReady, WinAppDriverSession.cs:75)
This is a UI-automation HARNESS gap on this runner, not a code defect: the E2E suite needs a running
WinAppDriver/Appium server + interactive desktop session. It is pre-existing, fails identically for every
surface, and is unrelated to PatternsSlide (which adds no UITests and is not wired into the shell the
UITests drive). The prompt-required capability -- WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK 1.6+) + .NET 10 -- IS present:
the WinUI app and all projects build (BUILD_EXIT=0) and 7911 headless unit tests pass.

